  "response": "**Setting up the count**\n\nLet A = multiples of 3, B = multiples of 5, up to 1000.\n\n**Step 1: Count divisible by 3 or 5**\n- ⌊1000/3⌋ = 333\n- ⌊1000/5⌋ = 200\n- ⌊1000/15⌋ = 66 (divisible by both 3 and 5)\n\n|A ∪ B| = 333 + 200 − 66 = **467**\n\n**Step 2: Subtract those among these that are also divisible by 7**\n\nWe need |(A ∪ B) ∩ (div by 7)| = |(3&7)| + |(5&7)| − |(3&5&7)|\n- Divisible by 21: ⌊1000/21⌋ = 47\n- Divisible by 35: ⌊1000/35⌋ = 28\n- Divisible by 105: ⌊1000/105⌋ = 9\n\nSo overlap = 47 + 28 − 9 = 66\n\n**Step 3: Final count**\n\n467 − 66 = **401**\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 401",
